$(i + 0.5)^2 + (j + 0.5)^2 \le R^2$.
Let $x = i + 0.5$ and $y = j + 0.5$. Since $i, j \ge 0$, $x, y \ge 0.5$.
We need $x^2 + y^2 \le R^2$.
This is equivalent to $y \le \sqrt{R^2 - x^2}$.
So $j + 0.5 \le \sqrt{R^2 - (i + 0.5)^2}$.
$j \le \sqrt{R^2 - (i + 0.5)^2} - 0.5$.
Let $val = \sqrt{R^2 - (i + 0.5)^2} - 0.5$.
