If we just sort all possible marginal costs, there are potentially too many units. The maximum number of units for a single product could be around $\sqrt{M/P_i} \approx \sqrt{10^{18}/1} = 10^9$. Total units could be huge. We cannot list all marginal costs.

However, notice that the marginal costs for product $i$ are $P_i, 3P_i, 5P_i, \dots$.
