We want to maximize $\sum x_i$ subject to $\sum P_i x_i^2 \le M$.
Using Lagrange multipliers or simple intuition:
To minimize cost for a fixed total count $S$, we should distribute the units such that the marginal costs are equalized.
The marginal cost for product $i$ at count $x_i$ is $(2x_i - 1)P_i$.
So we want $(2x_i - 1)P_i \approx \lambda$ for all $i$ where $x_i > 0$.
